## A shooter with a setting to pay attention to

4A Games develops METRO 2039, and Steam lists Deep Silver as the publisher. 4A Games describes it as a first-person shooter set in post-apocalyptic Moscow and its Metro. That gives the watchlist a clear focus: how the game connects its atmosphere and storytelling with the decisions you make while moving through a dangerous place.

When considering it, look beyond the busiest action sequence. An ordinary stretch of exploration can tell you more about the pacing you will spend time with than a short collection of dramatic encounters.

## How this title sits next to earlier Metro games

Metro games have usually mixed tight underground spaces with surface stretches, scarcity, and story pressure. METRO 2039 is a new listing, not a remaster page for Metro Exodus or the earlier PC releases. Bookmark [the Steam app for METRO 2039](https://store.steampowered.com/app/2590240/?l=english) rather than an older Metro store page if you are tracking this project.

If you already know the series, decide what you want from the next entry: a familiar tone, a new protagonist focus, or a different balance of stealth and firefights. Those preferences help you judge trailers without treating every dramatic shot as a promise about the whole campaign.

## The release information to bookmark

The Steam listing currently gives 4 February 2027 as its release date. That was checked on 18 November 2026; later publisher announcements may change the plan. Use the linked listing to verify availability in your region.

Do not treat this feature as a final compatibility verdict. Compare the current complete requirements and any installation notes with your own computer before a purchase, especially if your decision depends on specific graphics settings.

## Practical takeaways before the next reveal

- Prefer longer exploration footage over montage-only trailers when you care about pacing.
- Check whether the store page you opened is app 2590240, not an older Metro title.
- Treat 4 February 2027 as the publisher’s dated listing, not a guarantee against later moves.
- Leave performance claims for coverage that names a tested build and hardware.

We have not played METRO 2039 or benchmarked it. For now, keep demonstrated gameplay and expectations separate.

